messages:
mike: Heads-up: Riverside Finance pilot kickoff tomorrow. They want a streaming connector (SSE) that uses function/tool calls to enrich transactions and emits a strictly-typed transaction_output object. Also asking for a predictable pilot price and BYOK options. Can someone draft a minimal handshake + sample SDK snippet we can hand to their engineers?

tara: I can do the handshake. For SSE we require Authorization: Bearer <KEY> and recommend X-Client-Id. Example handshake: 
```bash
curl -N -H "Authorization: Bearer $REDWOOD_KEY" -H "X-Client-Id: riverside-connector" "https://api.redwood.ai/v1/streams?model=rlhf-stream-1&mode=function_calling"
```

mike: Good. They specifically want to call an internal fraud_check tool from the stream and get back a structured fraud_result that we should merge into the final transaction_output. Does the SDK support adapter wiring?

dilip: Yes. SDKs include a local tool adapter pattern. Quick TS example for registering a tool handler: 
```ts
import {StreamingClient} from '@redwood/sdks';
const client = new StreamingClient({apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY});
client.on('tool_call', async (event) => {
  if (event.tool === 'fraud_check') {
    const result = await callInternalFraudService(event.payload);
    client.send({type: 'tool_result', id: event.id, payload: result});
  }
});
```

tara: For output validation we recommend sharing a JSON Schema they must adhere to. Suggested minimal transaction_output schema: 
```json
{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","title":"transaction_output","type":"object","properties":{"tx_id":{"type":"string"},"amount":{"type":"number"},"currency":{"type":"string"},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["authorized","declined"]},"fraud":{"type":"object","properties":{"score":{"type":"number"},"action":{"type":"string"}},"required":["score"]}},"required":["tx_id","amount","currency","status"]}
```

mike: Pricing: they want a pilot cap with bursts up to 200 QPS and steady 30 QPS. Any quick recommendation for a pilot plan?

infra: For predictable pilot billing we usually provision a small Dedicated pool with reserved hours for the pilot duration. Suggest 2x smaller than peak to allow burst with autoscale/burst credits. Ops can run a quick cost model; pinged them. Hosted is possible but can spike cost.

security-bot: Security checklist: BYOK (customer-managed KMS) supported on Dedicated/Private; SSO via SAML/OIDC; ephemeral API keys recommended for connectors; network options: IP allowlist or VPC peering. For pen-test/SOC2 docs, request via security request form. Expect legal review ~2-3 weeks if BYOK/pen-test involved.

tara: Also note: if they need low-latency SLA for authorization (<100ms p50), include that in ask; Dedicated SLA necessary.

mike: Any enterprise blockers we should flag before call?

dilip: Blockers: 1) If they require air-gapped on-prem deploy, timeline ~6w. 2) KMS key ceremony / BYOK legal approvals; 3) Network ops availability for VPC peering (depends on cloud provider). 4) Schema freeze for structured outputs (we should lock fields before integration).

mike: Perfect. Can someone bundle a 1-page runbook + curl/py/ts snippets and an estimated pilot pricing slide? I want to send to their engineering lead pre-call.

tara: Will assemble runbook + minimal sample repo (py + ts examples) and post link here.

infra: Created ticket: RED-8122 presales/riverside - streaming POC & BYOK. Attaching ops sizing request.

sales-bot: Meeting created on calendar: Riverside - Tech kickoff (10:30 AM PT). Invite sent to their eng lead.

mike: Thanks team — see you on the call.
